    <section class="faq-page" data-anim="fade">
      <div class="container">
      <div class="faq-group" data-anim="up">
        <h2>Residential</h2>
        <div class="faq light">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">What do we actually design in a house?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Living, kitchen, wardrobes and the quiet room — as one instrument. You approve how the family lives, not a moodboard.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Do you invent a layout in 3D?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">No. Space is planned first. 3D happens after — or not at all if you only need drawings.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Can 3D-only be the whole job?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Yes. Stills, walkthrough or 360 can be a complete engagement. BOQ and the mill are optional.</div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-group" data-anim="up">
        <h2>Commercial</h2>
        <div class="faq light">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">What is an office brief at Woodex?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Arrival, focus and the room where you demo. The mural comes last.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Do you do software houses?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Yes. Focus first, culture second. Named outputs: plan, stills, BOQ if you want site.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Pharmacy and clinic?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Waiting, counter, dispensary. Calm rooms that have to work on a Saturday. Wellstar is the named path.</div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-group" data-anim="up">
        <h2>Retail</h2>
        <div class="faq light">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">What are you approving in a shop?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Enter, pause, pay — a path that can sell. Not a warehouse with lights.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Showrooms?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">The walk and the table where the decision happens.</div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-group" data-anim="up">
        <h2>Fit-out</h2>
        <div class="faq light">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">What is fit-out at Woodex?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Two routes: Woodex-designed, or your drawings (we review first). You approve the scope in writing, then the site.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Turnkey?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Design through install when that is the brief. Budget and BOQ sit inside Plan and Build.</div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-group" data-anim="up">
        <h2>Renovation</h2>
        <div class="faq light">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">What happens first on a renovation?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Survey. You approve a layout the existing bones can hold — before 3D.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Live homes and shops?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Phasing so the house or the counter can keep working.</div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-group" data-anim="up">
        <h2>Visualization</h2>
        <div class="faq light">
          <article class="faq-item is-open">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">What is a still for?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">A still is a meeting. You are approving a room, not a plan.</div>
          </article>
          <article class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-q" type="button">Walkthrough vs stills?<span class="plus"></span></button>
            <div class="faq-a">Stills first. Walkthrough or 360 only if the path through the building matters.</div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  
